================================================================================
Sotto — in-browser tutor (O2-B slice 1) evidence
Run: 2026-09-05 (local time 2026-09-04 evening), macOS 15 / M-series, Chromium
     via Playwright 1.62, headless, --enable-unsafe-webgpu --use-angle=metal.

WHAT RAN WHERE
  STT ran on **WebGPU**, not the wasm fallback. The worker tries webgpu first
  and reports which one won; both lines below say `webgpu`. No second attempt
  was needed, so the wasm path is NOT exercised by this log.

  Model: onnx-community/whisper-base, encoder fp16 + decoder_model_merged q8,
  ~95 MB, downloaded from the Hugging Face hub on an explicit tap.

MEASURED
  stt_load_ms = 3884 ms   (cold pipeline construction, weights already cached)
  stt_ms      = 1049 ms   for a 2.7 s speech segment, on WebGPU
  download    = 29.3 s    for the 95 MB model over this connection

SCOPE
  Slice 1 is the STT stage only. There is no tutor reply yet: the LLM (slice 2)
  and TTS (slice 3) stages are stubbed behind the worker protocol. The run
  therefore asserts a LEARNER caption, state transitions, and the opt-in
  download flow — nothing about a tutor answer.

  Transcript was "¿Qué significa la palabra cigarrara?" for a spoken
  "¿Qué significa la palabra cigarra?" — whisper-base's ending, not a bug in
  the pipeline. whisper-small would fix it but its q8 export is ~249 MB.

COMMAND
  pnpm --filter @sotto/client web:export && node apps/client/e2e/browser-tutor.mjs
